eighth of it for state slots); it replaces the four explicit Host capacity options
       --host-cache-max-mib N caps what --auto-host-cache pins, for machines whose memory other tenants share (default: no cap)
       --host-cache-percent N caps it at N% (1-100) of the machine's total memory (or its container's limit) whatever is free at startup; the smallest of this, the cap and the free memory less the reserve applies. With vision on, the reserve also covers --media-cache-mib and --media-live-mib
       --default-thinking-budget caps model-origin thinking for enabled requests; control tokens count toward the request output limit
       --preserve-thinking retains closed-turn assistant reasoning in later prompts
       --graft NAME=PATH loads a phantom-kv prefill graft (a safetensors container with a .json sidecar beside it); a request selecting it with "graft": "NAME" runs as if the graft's hidden turn preceded its own messages. Repeatable
       --default-graft NAME applies a loaded graft to every request that states none; a request opts out with "graft": ""
       --reasoning-effort is the effort of thinking-enabled requests that state none; request values override it; like request values, minimal runs as low and high/max as xhigh
       sampler defaults come from the loaded model and resolved thinking mode; server flags and request fields override individual values.
       --greedy forces temperature 0 (exact argmax).
       --version prints the build version and exits.

